common_passwords.txt.gz — bundled common/breached-password denylist (NIST SP 800-63B blocklist).

Source: SecLists — Passwords/Common-Credentials/100k-most-used-passwords-NCSC.txt
  https://github.com/danielmiessler/SecLists
  (NCSC UK top-100k, derived from the Have I Been Pwned breach corpus.)
License: MIT — SecLists, Copyright (c) 2018 Daniel Miessler. Full text below, reproduced
because MIT requires the copyright and permission notices travel with any copy.

Bundled subset, not the full list. Regeneration recipe:
  Take the source list, keep entries with MIN_PASSWORD_LENGTH <= len <= MAX_PASSWORD_LENGTH
  (see app/core/auth/password_policy.py — currently 8..128), casefold, de-duplicate, sort,
  then `gzip -9 -n` (the -n drops the timestamp/name so the blob is reproducible).
  Entries shorter than the minimum are unreachable (the length gate rejects them before the
  denylist is consulted), so only the reachable subset is shipped (~46k entries, ~442 KB raw
  → ~147 KB gzipped). If MIN_PASSWORD_LENGTH ever drops, regenerate from the full source.

